      "writtenOn": "2017-03-27T13:22:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe the following would be a better, more complete description.\n\nThe authorization scope, including either a project or a domain (Since v3.4). If both a domain and a project are specified, an HTTP 400 Bad Request will be returned, as a token cannot be simultaneously scoped to both a project and a domain. An id is sufficient to uniquely identify a project but if a project is specified by name, then the domain of the project must also be specified in order to uniquely identify the project. A domain scope may be specified by either the domain\u0027s id or name with equivalent results.",
